{"content":[{"c":["BOIL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Inflamed localized swelling on the skin. In modern medicine the term “boil” is restricted to a pus-filled swelling caused by infectious germs, usually staphylococci. The pus is a mixture of germs and white blood cells, which are the body’s defense against germs. Although painful, boils usually heal naturally after rupturing or being lanced. A more severe boil with several openings is called a carbuncle. If the infection goes deeper and injures internal organs or tissues, it is called an abscess and can even be fatal."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["In the Bible the word translated “boil” probably referred to a variety of skin diseases. The sixth plague that God inflicted on Egypt through Moses and Aaron was a plague of boils (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.9.9-11","r":"Exod.9.9-11","rawR":"Exod.9.9-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.9.9-11","value":"Exod.9.9-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 9:9-11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.28.27,35","r":"Deut.28.27,35","rawR":"Deut.28.27,35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.28.27,35","value":"Deut.28.27,35"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 28:27, 35"},") or blisters. Boils or skin eruptions of a certain type were described in the Mosaic health and sanitation code as one indication of leprosy (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.13.1-8,18-23","r":"Lev.13.1-8,18-23","rawR":"Lev.13.1-8,18-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.13.1-8,18-23","value":"Lev.13.1-8,18-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 13:1-8, 18-23"},"). Job’s “terrible case of boils from head to foot” (",{"href":"?bref=Job.2.7-8,12","r":"Job.2.7-8,12","rawR":"Job.2.7-8,12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.2.7-8,12","value":"Job.2.7-8,12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 2:7-8, 12"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") were probably too extensive to be boils in the modern sense; he may have had smallpox, psoriasis, tubercular leprosy, or some other disease accompanied by severe itching. King Hezekiah’s boil was probably a carbuncle (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.20.1-7","r":"2Kgs.20.1-7","rawR":"2Kgs.20.1-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.20.1-7","value":"2Kgs.20.1-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 20:1-7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.38.21","r":"Isa.38.21","rawR":"Isa.38.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.38.21","value":"Isa.38.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 38:21"},"). ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MedicineandMedicalPractice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Medicine and Medical Practice"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Disease_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Disease_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Disease_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Disease"},"; ",{"href":"?item=PlaguesuponEgypt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"PlaguesuponEgypt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"PlaguesuponEgypt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Plagues upon Egypt"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Boil","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ex 9:9-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.9.9-11","rawQueryValue":"Exod.9.9-11","sourceRefExact":"Exod.9.9-11"},{"anchorText":"Dt 28:27, 35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.28.27,35","rawQueryValue":"Deut.28.27,35","sourceRefExact":"Deut.28.27,35"},{"anchorText":"Lv 13:1-8, 18-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.13.1-8,18-23","rawQueryValue":"Lev.13.1-8,18-23","sourceRefExact":"Lev.13.1-8,18-23"},{"anchorText":"Jb 2:7-8, 12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.2.7-8,12","rawQueryValue":"Job.2.7-8,12","sourceRefExact":"Job.2.7-8,12"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 20:1-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.20.1-7","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.20.1-7","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.20.1-7"},{"anchorText":"Is 38:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.38.21","rawQueryValue":"Isa.38.21","sourceRefExact":"Isa.38.21"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"98edaa6d432d19227293510e62ee7762600aa6d188543dc12360bbaa5a7d5d96","sourceItemName":"Boil","sourceItemOrder":366,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Boil","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Boil","title":"Boil","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}